---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="Shop information" description="How the shop works: buying one-of-a-kind pieces, shipping, care, returns and breakages.">
  <section class="container page-head narrow">
    <h1 class="page-title">Shop information</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="section container narrow" aria-label="Shop information">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How the shop works</h2>
      <p>
        Every piece is one of a kind. Once it sells, it's gone. New work goes up on <a href={site.instagram.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram</a>
        first, then in the <a href="/shop/">shop</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pieces with a Buy button can be bought straight away. Checkout is handled securely by Stripe.
        For anything marked "Ask about this piece", <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a> and I'll
        reply with a price and shipping.
      </p>

      <h2>Shipping</h2>
      <p>
        I'm not shipping at the moment while I work on my next body of work. When shipping opens
        again, I'll post it here on the website.
      </p>

      <h2>Care</h2>
      <p>
        Crystalline surfaces are not food safe. Treat a crystalline piece as decorative, and keep
        food and drink off the crystalline glaze.
      </p>
      <p>
        Always wash pieces by hand. No dishwasher, microwave or oven. Use warm water, mild soap and a
        soft cloth, and dry the piece completely before putting it away. Avoid scouring pads and
        abrasive cleaners, which can dull the glaze.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lift pieces with both hands, by the body rather than the rim. Pierced pieces in particular
        are delicate around their openings. Keep pieces away from sudden changes in temperature,
        like hot water poured into a cold piece.
      </p>

      <h2>Returns</h2>
      <p>I don't accept returns. Please look over the photos and details carefully before buying.</p>

      <h2>Breakages</h2>
      <p>
        Every piece is packed carefully, but occasionally something goes astray or arrives broken.
        If that happens, please <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a> and we can arrange a refund, or
        a replacement if I have a similar piece. Each case is handled individually. Postal charges,
        return shipping costs, customs charges and handling fees are deducted from any refund due.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please check your shipping address before you order. If a wrong address is only noticed
        after the parcel has shipped, I'll always try to help, but I can't refund a parcel that is
        lost as a result. The same goes for parcels sent on to someone else after delivery: I can't
        cover loss or damage on that second journey.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Anything else, <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
